WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.844
The historical naming deck used family, word length, class, identity, and an optional modifier.

2
00:00:07.844 --> 00:00:14.532
Current CVA6 documentation separates pipeline stages from the product identifier.

3
00:00:14.532 --> 00:00:29.478
Be careful with its width notation: although the naming figure uses ILEN, the 32 or 64 in these names identifies the integer-register width, called XLEN in the RISC-V specification.

4
00:00:29.478 --> 00:00:33.441
It does not give the length of each instruction.

5
00:00:33.441 --> 00:00:41.368
RV64 uses 32-bit base instruction encodings and may also support 16-bit compressed instructions.

6
00:00:41.368 --> 00:00:49.460
The ISA term ILEN instead describes the maximum instruction length supported by an implementation.

